  exist, the binder [1mcreates a [38;5;153m<span class="field-error">[39m and inserts it after the input[0m. That fallback is the whole
  point: a new form needs [38;5;153mname[39m attributes and nothing else. Explicit placement stays available when a layout demands it.

  Each rendered error also sets [38;5;153maria-invalid="true"[39m and [38;5;153maria-describedby[39m on the input, pointing at its message. It's a
  few lines and it's the difference between an error a screen reader announces and one it doesn't.

  [1mClearing.[0m All messages clear at the start of every submit. Additionally, once a field has shown an error, typing in it
  clears [3mthat[0m field's message on [38;5;153minput[39m — it doesn't re-validate. Re-validating on every keystroke means telling someone
  their password is too short while they're still typing it.

  [1m[38;5;153mindex.html[0m also gains a small [38;5;153m<style>[39m block for [38;5;153m.field-error[39m (red, smaller text). The page currently has no CSS at
  all, so without it the messages render as unstyled black text indistinguishable from the form.

  [1m[38;5;153mapp.js[39m after the rewire:[0m

  [34mconst[39m LOGIN_SCHEMA = {
    [36musername[39m: { [36mlabel[39m: [31m"Username"[39m, [36mrequired[39m: [34mtrue[39m, [36mminLength[39m: [32m3[39m },
    [36mpassword[39m: { [36mlabel[39m: [31m"Password"[39m, [36mrequired[39m: [34mtrue[39m, [36mminLength[39m: [32m8[39m },
  };

  [34mFormValidation[39m.[33mbind[39m(document.[33mgetElementById[39m([31m"login-form"[39m), LOGIN_SCHEMA, [33m([39m{ username, password }) => {
    console.[33mlog[39m([31m"Login result:"[39m, [33mlogin[39m(username, password));
  });

  [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m is deleted, the hand-written [38;5;153mgetElementById[39m reads and the [38;5;153msubmit[39m listener go away, and [38;5;153mlogin()[39m /
  [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m are untouched. [38;5;153mindex.html[39m loads [38;5;153mvalidation.js[39m before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m via a second plain [38;5;153m<script src>[39m — no change
  to how the page loads.

  [1mOne thing to flag:[0m the login form currently enforces presence only. The schema above adds [38;5;153mminLength: 3[39m and [38;5;153mminLength:
[39m  [38;5;153m8[39m, which is [3mnew[0m behavior — a 4-character password that logs in today would be rejected. I think that's what you want
  from a validation layer, but it's a behavior change beyond pure extraction, so it's your call rather than mine.

  Does the binder look right, and do you want those minLength rules?

